course: dictionary
lesson: 14298
title: Short forms: Nov
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A short form is a shorter way to write a longer word. Nov is short for November, the eleventh month of the year. Short forms save space on forms, calendars and dates, and the full stop after them, as in «Nov.», shows that letters have been left out.
explain: You will see Nov on calendars and forms, such as «5 Nov» for Bonfire Night in the UK, which is also called Guy Fawkes Night. You may also see «Nov 11», which is Remembrance Day in the UK and Veterans Day in the USA.
explain: In your own school writing, write the month in full, like «We went to the zoo in November.», unless the space is very small. Use Nov only when you need to save room, such as in a table or on a form.
fact: Nov is an abbreviation, a short form of a longer word.
fact: Nov is short for November, the eleventh month of the year.
fact: «5 Nov» is Bonfire Night in the UK, also called Guy Fawkes Night.
fact: «Nov 11» is Remembrance Day in the UK and Veterans Day in the USA.
fact: In school writing, write November in full unless space is short.
exercise: What does Nov stand for? | *November | Monday | Novel | Nomad
exercise: «The fireworks lit up the sky on 5 Nov.» Which celebration is this? | Halloween | New Year's Day | *Bonfire Night | Easter
exercise: In your school writing, what should you do with the word Nov? | Leave the month out | Write it in capitals only | Always write it short | *Write November in full unless space is short
test: Which month is Nov short for? | Monday | *November | Novel | January
test: What is «Nov 11» in the UK? | *Remembrance Day | Mother's Day | Bonfire Night | Boxing Day
exam: In a story you write for school, which is the best choice? | Nov. | *November | nov | N11
